Let sign-out clear the searches, not just the watching

signOut() in AppShell already wipes four device-local stores, each with a
comment saying why: a school-lab browser must not hand the next student the
last one's progress, notes, streak or revision queue. ll_search_history_v1 was
not among them, and it is the one holding text the student TYPED — up to eight
queries, shown as chips under an empty search box, so the next person does not
even have to go looking.

The policy did not promise otherwise, so nothing on the page was false. It was
incomplete: section 4 enumerates how that list can be emptied, and sign-out now
belongs in that list, so the sentence names it.

The second half is a race the obvious fix would not have closed.
scheduleSearchMemory holds ONE module-level timer and deliberately survives
unmount, because a search the student clicked through within a second is
exactly the one worth keeping. That timer calls rememberSearch() on a delay, so
clearing only the stored list leaves the pending write to put the term straight
back about a second later, with nothing on screen to show it. Cancelling lives
in clearRecentSearches() rather than at the sign-out call site, so the Clear
button — which had the same hole — is fixed by the same line.

Both halves are mutation-checked, because a test that passes with the fix
removed proves nothing and this repository has been bitten by exactly that:
  * delete clearRecentSearches() from AppShell  -> 1 failed, 7 passed
  * delete the timer cancel from the helper      -> 3 failed, 29 passed
The sign-out pair follows the shape already in studentAccountExit.test.jsx: one
test that it clears on success, one that it does NOT clear when sign-out fails,
since wiping a student's own searches out from under a failed sign-out would be
the same bug pointed the other way.

Found while triaging a review of the reconcile; it was the only student-facing
item in that pass that survived checking against production.

